==Russian==

===Etymology===
Perhaps borrowed from {{bor|ru|fr|taffetas}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|туфта́}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|туфта́|n=sg|adj=туфто́вый}}

# {{lb|ru|slang}} [[bullshit]], [[nonsense]], [[poppycock]], [[rubbish]]
# {{lb|ru|slang}} [[fake]], [[fraud]]
## {{lb|ru|slang}} [[cheating|Cheating]] on [[quota]] or bureaucratic requirements, as for example in [[labour camp]]s, in state enterprises of planned economies, or in municipal affairs.
##* {{quote-book|ru|year=1975|author=w:Alexander Dolgun|title=Alexander Dolgun's Story: An American in the Gulag|page=173|publisher=Knopf
|passage=Thank God for Gorelov that day! He had been lucky and had received some food parcels from home, and had strategically given more than half of what he got to the brigadier. This got him both a lower quota, and a blind eye to his '''''tufta''''', his cheating on the quota.}}

